1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,823
The ten percent challenge.

2
00:00:01,823 --> 00:00:06,911
Our attempt to shrink a trained model below ten percent of its size, keep its behaviour on an

3
00:00:06,911 --> 00:00:10,577
exam it never saw, and teach it a new label from a few corrections.

4
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:16,694
The challenge asks for a model at most ten percent of the original size, counting every shipped

5
00:00:16,694 --> 00:00:16,963
byte.

6
00:00:16,963 --> 00:00:20,408
It must behave the same as the original on an exam it never saw.

7
00:00:20,408 --> 00:00:25,468
And it must learn from a few user corrections, without training its weights, and without a new

8
00:00:25,468 --> 00:00:26,544
head or side memory.

9
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:32,962
We start from a trained model and compress it without weight training, giving a packed artifact

10
00:00:32,962 --> 00:00:34,447
under ten percent of fp16.

11
00:00:34,447 --> 00:00:37,814
An answer command writes a skill word by greedy generation.

12
00:00:37,814 --> 00:00:43,065
A feedback command takes at most twenty five annotations and computes replacement values for

13
00:00:43,065 --> 00:00:44,036
existing tensors.

14
00:00:44,036 --> 00:00:49,458
The grown model is the same files plus that patch, and a locked exam, sealed by hash, is scored

15
00:00:49,458 --> 00:00:49,744
once.

16
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:51,067
Size.

17
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:57,085
Our filed entry L1 is 7.16 percent of Qwen three eight B in fp sixteen, with the patch, code

18
00:00:57,085 --> 00:00:59,179
and calibration prompts counted.

19
00:00:59,179 --> 00:01:05,197
The alternate L9b, a pruned three bit Qwen three point five thirty five B A three B, is 9.70

20
00:01:05,197 --> 00:01:07,421
percent with its feedback carrier.

21
00:01:07,421 --> 00:01:08,533
The limit is ten.

22
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:10,587
Feedback on L1.

23
00:01:10,587 --> 00:01:16,858
Twenty five annotations teach the new label Recipe to 90.9 percent of a locked set of 164

24
00:01:16,858 --> 00:01:20,100
unseen requests, through the shipped commands.

25
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,989
Neighbouring labels stay at 99.7 percent.

26
00:01:22,989 --> 00:01:27,498
Shuffled labels, wrong labels and empty feedback all teach zero.

27
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,940
The alternate L9b.

28
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:37,459
Over eight draws, real feedback teaches 75.8 percent on average, while shuffled labels average

29
00:01:37,459 --> 00:01:40,738
16.0 percent, with some draws up to 39.6.

30
00:01:40,738 --> 00:01:48,097
Retention against the original model is 99.47 to 99.55 percent across three quantizer draws.

31
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:57,515
L1 at a glance: 7.16 percent of the size, 90.9 percent teach on the new label, and 99.7 percent

32
00:01:57,515 --> 00:01:59,906
of neighbouring items kept.

33
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:01,342
Caveats.

34
00:02:01,342 --> 00:02:03,445
The exam is ours, not the maintainer's.

35
00:02:03,445 --> 00:02:07,760
L1 starts from a released one bit model, so the compression is its makers' work.

36
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:11,752
Three of the nine passes rest on readings the maintainer has not ruled on.

37
00:02:11,752 --> 00:02:14,449
And the task is one narrow task with seven labels.

38
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:20,198
Reports, manifests and raw results are in the repo.

